From a3007adc9270a5b5e2b5f47cbdc92ae1c82509e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mayor <git@hough.ink>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 14:23:36 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 65/67] witness: prune stale merge-requested cleanup wisps so
 merged polecats reclaim (feryn-ipm9 follow-up)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

hasPendingMR's Check 1 treated ANY open merge-requested cleanup wisp as a pending
MR and refused to reclaim the polecat (the gt-6a9d reap guard). But nothing closes
that wisp after the merge lands: createCleanupWisp makes it at POLECAT_DONE, the
refinery merges, gt mq post-merge closes the MR bead + source issue — but the
cleanup wisp stays open forever. The reap then refuses to nuke the (fully done)
polecat every patrol, permanently wedging its slot. Observed live on feryn: all 11
slots pinned by stale hq-wisp-* cleanup wisps whose source beads were already
closed; check-recovery said SAFE_TO_NUKE while the reap said "MR pending" — the
exact divergence, since check-recovery (DecideWorkstate) never consults the wisp.

Fix: a merge-requested wisp only blocks reclaim while its source issue is still
unmerged. The source issue closing is the authoritative "merge landed" signal
(gt mq post-merge closes it only after a successful merge). mergeRequestedWispPendingIssue
parses each open merge-requested wisp's "Issue: <id>", and when that issue is
closed/reaped it closes the stale wisp in-place (breaking the deadlock and stopping
the leak) instead of counting it pending. Fails safe on any lookup/parse error
(stays pending) so a transient failure never trades a false "merge done" for lost
work. Applied to both hasPendingMR and hasPendingMRFromSnapshot.

Test: TestHasPendingMRPrunesStaleMergeRequestedWisp (closed source issue → not
pending + wisp closed). Full witness package green.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
